{{Infobox religious building|religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]]|religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]]|religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]]| religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] | name = Rokusho Shrine | image = [[File:Rokusho-jinja (Ichikawa), Haiden.jpg|250px|thumb|Haiden of Rokusho Shrine]] | coordinates = {{WikidataCoord|display=inline,title}} | location = Suwada 2-22-7, Ichikawa City, Chiba Prefecture, Japan | deity = * {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=}} (Ōnamuchi no Mikoto) * {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi|qq=}} * {{ill|Susanoo|1=Susanoo-no-Mikoto|ja|素盞嗚尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Susanoo|13=User:Immanuelle/Susanoo-no-Mikoto|qq=}} * {{ill|Ōmiyame-no-Kami|ja|大宮売神|1=Ōmiya-no-Me|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōmiyame-no-Kami|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōmiya-no-Me|qq=}} * Furu no Mitama * {{ill|Ninigi|ja|彦火瓊々杵尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ninigi|qq=}} | established = Unknown (traditional date during the reign of Emperor Keikō) | festivals = {{ill|October 20|ja|10月20日|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/October 20|qq=}} }}
'''Rokusho Shrine''' ({{nihongo|六所神社|ろくしょじんじゃ}}) is a [[Shinto shrine]] located in {{ill|Ichikawa|ja|市川市|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ichikawa|qq=}}, Chiba Prefecture, Japan. Historically, it served as the {{nihongo|Sōja|総社}} (provincial general shrine) of {{ill|Shimōsa Province|ja|下総国|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimōsa Province|qq=}} and was classified as a [[village shrine]] ({{nihongo|sonsha|村社}}) under the [[modern system of Ranked Shinto shrines]].
== Overview == In ancient Japan, {{ill|Provincial Governor|ja|国司|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Provincial Governor|qq=}} would visit all the shrines in their province in order of importance. To streamline this practice, a single "general shrine" was established near the provincial capital, where the province’s deities were enshrined collectively. Rokusho Shrine is regarded as the Sōja of {{ill|Shimōsa Province|ja|下総国|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimōsa Province|qq=}}.
Originally located at the site of present-day Ichikawa City Sports Center, the shrine was moved to its current location in {{ill|1886|ja|明治19th year|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/1886|qq=}} due to the construction of a military training ground. The new site was chosen because it was the residence of the shrine's priest.
== Enshrined Deities == The shrine enshrines six deities: * {{ill|Ōkuninushi|ja|大己貴尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|qq=}} (Ōnamuchi no Mikoto) * {{ill|Izanagi|ja|伊弉諾尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi|qq=}} * {{ill|Susanoo|1=Susanoo-no-Mikoto|ja|素盞嗚尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Susanoo|13=User:Immanuelle/Susanoo-no-Mikoto|qq=}} * {{ill|Ōmiyame-no-Kami|ja|大宮売神|1=Ōmiya-no-Me|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōmiyame-no-Kami|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōmiya-no-Me|qq=}} * Furu no Mitama * {{ill|Ninigi|ja|彦火瓊々杵尊|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ninigi|qq=}}
== festivals == The following festivals are held annually at the shrine: * New Year’s festival ({{nihongo|Gantan-sai|元旦祭}}) – January 1 * {{nihongo|Setsubun festival|節分祭}} – February * {{nihongo|Kinensai|祈年祭}} – February 17 * {{nihongo|Ōharae ceremony|大祓式}} – June 30 and December 31 * Grand festival ({{nihongo|Taisai|大祭}}) – October 20 * Labor Thanksgiving festival ({{nihongo|Kinrō Kansha-sai|勤労感謝祭}}) – November 23 * {{ill|Shichi-Go-San|ja|七五三才祝|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shichi-Go-San|qq=}} – Sunday before November 15
== Historical Significance == The shrine was traditionally located at {{nihongo|Shimōsa Sōja Ruins|下総総社跡}}, believed to be the site of the provincial capital of Shimōsa. Excavations in the area have uncovered remains of pit dwellings from the early {{ill|Heian period|ja|平安時代|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Heian period|qq=}}, suggesting that the site served as the Sōja from that time.
The current location was selected after the shrine’s relocation in the {{ill|Meiji period|ja|明治|lt=Meiji period|1=Meiji era|2=ja|3=明治|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Meiji period|qq=}}.
== Cultural Properties == === Ichikawa City Designated Cultural Properties === * '''Shimōsa Sōja Ruins''': Designated as a historic site by Ichikawa City in 1975.
== Access == * '''location''': Suwada 2-22-7, Ichikawa City, Chiba Prefecture. * '''By Train''': ** 11-minute walk from {{ill|Ichikawa-Mama Station|ja|市川真間駅|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ichikawa-Mama Station|qq=}} on the {{ill|Keisei Main Line|ja|京成本線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Keisei Main Line|qq=}}. ** 18-minute walk from {{ill|Ichikawa Station|ja|市川駅|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ichikawa Station|qq=}} on the {{ill|Sōbu Main Line|ja|総武本線|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sōbu Main Line|qq=}}.
== Nearby Sites == * {{ill|Shimōsa Kokubunji|ja|下総国分寺|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shimōsa Kokubunji|qq=}} – A historical Buddhist temple site.
